874:
(a) Games. It shall be unlawful for any person to take part in or abet the playing of any games involving thrown or otherwise propelled objects such as balls, stones, arrows, javelins, drones or model airplanes except in areas set apart for such forms of recreation. The playing of rough or potentially dangerous games such as football, baseball and soccer is prohibited except on the fields, courts or areas provided therefore.
(b) Camping. It shall be unlawful for any person to set up tents, shacks or any other temporary shelter for the purpose of overnight camping, nor shall any person leave in a park after closing hours any movable structure or special vehicle to be used, or that could be used, for such purpose, such as a house trailer, camp trailer, camp wagon or the like unless permitted by the director of parks and recreation.
(c) Fires. It shall be unlawful for any person to build or attempt to build a fire except in such areas and under such regulations as may be designated by the director of parks and recreation. No person shall drop, throw or otherwise scatter lighted matches, burning cigarettes or cigars, tobacco paper or other flammable material within any park area or on a highway, road or street abutting or contiguous thereto.
(d) Animals. It shall be unlawful to bring any animal into any park, except dogs as expressly allowed by this paragraph (d). Dogs may be brought to parks and kept there by their owners in accordance with all of the following:
(1) No dogs, except for service animals, as defined by the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), shall be allowed: (i) indoors, (ii) inside any fence other than a fence surrounding the entire park, (iii) within 30 feet of any athletic field, playground equipment, or swimming pool;
(2) No dangerous dog or vicious dog as defined by the Georgia Responsible Dog Ownership Law, O.C.G.A. §§ 4-8-1 through 4-8-33, shall be allowed;
(3) No dog shall remain in a park after having exhibited aggressive behavior toward any person or animal at the park or after having damaged personal property at the park;
(4) No dog shall be brought to or remain in a park without wearing a visible dog license; the dog handler shall produce vaccination documents upon request by city staff or security personnel;
(5) Dogs in parks must be leashed, under the control of their handler and in view of their handler at all times; no leash shall be longer than six feet while in use; no dog shall be tethered while in any park;
(6) No dog handler shall be younger than 16 years of age; no handler shall supervise more than two dogs at one time;
(7) Every dog handler shall remove and properly dispose of his dog's waste;
(8) Every dog handler shall prevent his dogs from digging holes, and shall fill any holes dug;
(9) Every dog handler shall be liable for any damage or injury inflicted by any dog in his possession.
(e) Motor vehicles. It shall be unlawful for any person to operate a motor vehicle within any area of a public park, playground or recreational facility if operation within such an area is prohibited by any clearly posted sign or notice in such area erected under the authority of the director of parks and recreation or the mayor and council.
(f) Sales. It shall be unlawful for any person to vend, sell, peddle or offer for sale any commodity or article within any park unless permitted by the director of parks and recreation.
(g) Alcoholic beverages. It shall be unlawful for any person within any park to have in his possession, custody or control any alcoholic beverage of any kind whatsoever, except at the West Pines Golf Course.
(h) Signs. It shall be unlawful for anyone to paste, glue, tack or otherwise post any sign, placard, advertisement or inscription whatever upon and within public parks or playgrounds and recreational facilities unless same is permitted by the director of parks and recreation.
(Code 1977, § 17½-21; Ord. No. O-96-50, §§ 1, 2, 10-21-96; Ord. No. O-05-40, § 1, 7-5-05; Ord. No. O-2012-33, § 3, 7-2-12; Ord. No. O-2019-72, § 1, 12-16-19; Ord. No. O-2022-12, §§ 3, 4, 3-21-22)

